{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":175.38,"success_pct":0.995},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [cc reliability defense-in-depth for the prefix bug] In layers/uia.py: (1) set_value verify block (around lines 744-751): currently \"if actual is not None:\" means when get_value returns None (Qt has no ValuePattern) the whole verify is SKIPPED and set_value silently returns success — this is how \"булочкапривет...\" passed as success=True. Make it fail-closed: when get_value returns None, do NOT return success silently; raise ValueError(\"set_value verify: could not read field value, refusing to report success\") so the supervisor escalates to a vision re-check. Also, when clear=True, after _clear_field_content read the field back and if still non-empty retry the clear up to 2 more times before typing (concatenation guard). (2) _set_value_with_keyboard_fallback (around lines 560-580) currently types WITHOUT clearing — add _clear_field_content() after SetFocus()+settle and before _type_text_unicode, with a read-back. Add unit tests: get_value None -\u003e set_value raises (no silent success); get_value \"булочкапривет...\" vs expected \"привет...\" with clear=True -\u003e ValueError; keyboard-fallback over a field pre-populated with \"булочка\" with text=\"привет\" yields exactly \"привет\" (not \"булочкапривет\").","commit":"ba0b9484075fe855940df546d9e85a3b71c30ad0","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-16T05:34:58.7860366Z"}
