{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":171.8,"success_pct":0.995},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [cc reliability ROOT FIX — over-strict foreground abort forces vision mis-send] In layers/uia.py _ensure_element_window_foreground (~704-712) and ensure_hwnd_foreground: when com_element.CurrentNativeWindowHandle is 0 or None — which is NORMAL for Qt child controls such as Telegram\u0027s search box and message composer (they are not separate top-level windows) — do NOT return False/abort. Instead resolve the element\u0027s TOP-LEVEL window: walk up the UIA tree via the control-view TreeWalker (GetParentElement) until an ancestor has a non-zero CurrentNativeWindowHandle, then GetAncestor(GA_ROOT) on it, and bring THAT top-level window to foreground. Only return False if no ancestor with a native window handle exists at all. ROOT CAUSE being fixed: currently set_value and invoke_element abort with \"cannot bring element window hwnd=None to foreground\" for every child Edit (nwh=0), which forces escalation to the vision path; vision then types the search query into the wrong field and an Enter sends a bogus \"Булочка\" message. Fixing foreground resolution keeps set_value on the reliable uia path. Unit test: a fake child element with CurrentNativeWindowHandle=0 whose parent chain yields an ancestor with a valid top-level hwnd -\u003e _ensure_element_window_foreground returns (True, top_level_hwnd), not (False, None); element with no native-window ancestor -\u003e (False, None).","commit":"ba0b9484075fe855940df546d9e85a3b71c30ad0","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-16T06:06:14.9393456Z"}
