{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":167.04,"success_pct":0.995},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [cc reliability ROOT FIX — disambiguation must respect the step\u0027s intended role, not just focus] In layers/uia.py _disambiguate_edits / find_element relaxation (~378-408): the current \"prefer CurrentHasKeyboardFocus==True\" rule can wrongly pick the bottom message composer when the step actually wants the SEARCH box (because the composer often holds keyboard focus once a chat is open). Make disambiguation role/position aware: accept a hint of the requested role (search vs message) derived from the step\u0027s automation_id/name (e.g. names/ids containing \u0027search\u0027/\u0027поиск\u0027 vs \u0027message\u0027/\u0027сообщение\u0027/composer) OR from vertical position. When the step targets a SEARCH field, prefer the candidate in the TOP region of the window; when it targets the MESSAGE composer, prefer the BOTTOM region. Use CurrentHasKeyboardFocus only as a tie-break AMONG candidates of the same role/region, never to override a clear role/position signal. ROOT CAUSE: relaxed find matches any Edit and \"prefer focused\" then routes the search query into the focused composer, which gets sent as \"Булочка\". Unit test: two Edits, one top-region named like a search box (unfocused) and one bottom-region composer (focused); a search-intent find returns the TOP one; a message-intent find returns the BOTTOM/focused one.","commit":"6f62bcee88badd6e77900a4e3110a810480a1bc8","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-16T06:25:13.2241448Z"}
