{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":28.7,"success_pct":0.005},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [cc reliability ROOT FIX — over-strict foreground abort forces vision mis-send] In layers/uia.py _ensure_element_window_foreground (~704-712) and ensure_hwnd_foreground: when com_element.CurrentNativeWindowHandle is 0 or None — which is NORMAL for Qt child controls such as Telegram\u0027s search box and message composer (they are not separate top-level windows) — do NOT return False/abort. Instead resolve the element\u0027s TOP-LEVEL window: walk up the UIA tree via the control-view TreeWalker (GetParentElement) until an ancestor has a non-zero CurrentNativeWindowHandle, then GetAncestor(GA_ROOT) on it, and bring THAT top-level window to foreground. Only return False if no ancestor with a native window handle exists at all. ROOT CAUSE being fixed: currently set_value and invoke_element abort with \"cannot bring element window hwnd=None to foreground\" for every child Edit (nwh=0), which forces escalation to the vision path; vision then types the search query into the wrong field and an Enter sends a bogus \"Булочка\" message. Fixing foreground resolution keeps set_value on the reliable uia path. Unit test: a fake child element with CurrentNativeWindowHandle=0 whose parent chain yields an ancestor with a valid top-level hwnd -\u003e _ensure_element_window_foreground returns (True, top_level_hwnd), not (False, None); element with no native-window ancestor -\u003e (False, None).","after_turns":35,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":200.5,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-16T06:06:14.9393456Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-17T23:00:39.0593720Z","commit":"ba0b9484075fe855940df546d9e85a3b71c30ad0"}
{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":39.68,"success_pct":0.005},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [cc reliability ROOT FIX — disambiguation must respect the step\u0027s intended role, not just focus] In layers/uia.py _disambiguate_edits / find_element relaxation (~378-408): the current \"prefer CurrentHasKeyboardFocus==True\" rule can wrongly pick the bottom message composer when the step actually wants the SEARCH box (because the composer often holds keyboard focus once a chat is open). Make disambiguation role/position aware: accept a hint of the requested role (search vs message) derived from the step\u0027s automation_id/name (e.g. names/ids containing \u0027search\u0027/\u0027поиск\u0027 vs \u0027message\u0027/\u0027сообщение\u0027/composer) OR from vertical position. When the step targets a SEARCH field, prefer the candidate in the TOP region of the window; when it targets the MESSAGE composer, prefer the BOTTOM region. Use CurrentHasKeyboardFocus only as a tie-break AMONG candidates of the same role/region, never to override a clear role/position signal. ROOT CAUSE: relaxed find matches any Edit and \"prefer focused\" then routes the search query into the focused composer, which gets sent as \"Булочка\". Unit test: two Edits, one top-region named like a search box (unfocused) and one bottom-region composer (focused); a search-intent find returns the TOP one; a message-intent find returns the BOTTOM/focused one.","after_turns":32,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":206.72,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-16T06:25:13.2241448Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-17T23:00:42.1906947Z","commit":"6f62bcee88badd6e77900a4e3110a810480a1bc8"}
