{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":39.64,"success_pct":0.005},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [cc reliability — intermittent comtypes segfault blocks runs] cc segfaults (process exit 139, comtypes COM access-violation) on roughly every run, during/after UIA tree reads of Telegram (Qt). Harden the UIAutomation COM lifetime in layers/uia.py: call CoInitializeEx(None, COINIT_APARTMENTTHREADED) once before the comtypes CUIAutomation client is first created (ignore RPC_E_CHANGED_MODE; guard against double-init), create the IUIAutomation client a single time as a module-level singleton reused across all find/observe calls (not constructed per call), and release cached _com_element references deterministically at end of a run rather than leaving them for interpreter-shutdown GC. Do not change find/observe selection logic. Add a smoke test that builds the UIA client and walks a small element tree in a 20-iteration loop asserting no crash and stable results.","after_turns":29,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":207.52,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-16T06:46:22.6837985Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-17T23:00:46.9771228Z","commit":"6f62bcee88badd6e77900a4e3110a810480a1bc8"}
