{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":59.81,"success_pct":0.005},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [cc reliability — fix regression from the segfault hardening] In layers/uia.py line 204 the COM-init call is `comtypes.CoInitializeEx(None, _COINIT_APARTMENTTHREADED)` which passes TWO positional args, but comtypes.CoInitializeEx accepts only ONE (the coinit flags). So EVERY uia call now raises \"TypeError: CoInitializeEx() takes from 0 to 1 positional arguments but 2 were given\", breaking all UIA find_element/set_value/invoke_element (each falls through to vision and the task fails). FIX: change line 204 to `comtypes.CoInitializeEx(_COINIT_APARTMENTTHREADED)` (single positional arg). Also broaden the except so a bad signature degrades gracefully: change `except AttributeError` to `except (AttributeError, TypeError)` falling back to comtypes.CoInitialize(). Do NOT remove the singleton-client / COM-lifetime hardening from the segfault fix — only correct the call signature. Verify with a real uia find_element OR a unit test exercising the COM-init path: assert NO \"CoInitializeEx() takes from 0 to 1 positional arguments\" TypeError is raised; the existing segfault smoke test still passes.","after_turns":24,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":223.63,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-16T07:31:59.7259579Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-17T23:00:48.8828100Z","commit":"be39f087c6cc3825628b5800fb0f0aa4bb9902c2"}
