{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":118.18,"success_pct":0.005},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [cc reliability — first-char doubling polish] In the vision type-into-field path, the typed message can come out with a doubled FIRST character (observed live: \"Ккак дела у тебя…\" instead of \"Как дела…\") because vision.type_text (layers/vision.py:414) types WITHOUT clearing the field first (unlike uia.set_value which does Ctrl+A+Delete) and starts typing immediately after click_at with no settle, so a residual/doubled leading char survives. FIX in layers/executor.py _vision_find_click_type (around line 482, the vision click+type fallback for a field): before calling vision.type_text on a message/composer field, (1) add a short settle sleep (~0.15s) after click_at so the click/focus-change finishes; (2) clear the field with Ctrl+A then Delete (win32 keybd_event, same as uia._clear_field_content) to remove any residual/doubled char; (3) then type; (4) after typing, if a UIA get_value read-back (via the apartment thread) is available and the value differs from the intended text by a doubled leading char, clear and retype ONCE. Do NOT change uia.set_value. Add tests/test that a field pre-populated with a stray leading char, then vision-typed \"Как дела\", yields exactly \"Как дела\" (no \"Ккак\").","after_turns":10,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":279.26,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-16T11:53:37.2618854Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-17T23:01:05.7001294Z","commit":"688ca961ef84ad5ccb315b4ca1ac4058e8cdde20"}
