{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":153.14,"success_pct":0.99},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] Neutralize the old direct deep-audit backlog filing in tools/audit.ps1 so unverified deep findings can no longer bypass the adversarial VERIFY stage. Small surgical change + test + commit. Do NOT touch the static-audit filing path.\n\n[[NORMAL]]\n\n[operator] Context: tools/audit.ps1 function Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog (starts line 1441) files ONLY deep-LLM findings (DeepCodexResult/DeepClaudeResult/DeepModelAgentResults) directly to the backlog, bypassing the new VERIFY pipeline. It returns [pscustomobject]@{ deepFiled; deepCodexCount; deepClaudeCount; deepModelAgentCount }. The call site (~line 1881) reads those four properties. audit.ps1 has a main-guard at the bottom (if InvocationName -ne \u0027.\u0027) so dot-sourcing is SAFE (main does not run).\n\nMake these changes to tools/audit.ps1 (do NOT break static-audit filing, which is a separate path):\n\n1) Add a small pure helper near Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog:\n   function Test-AuditDirectDeepFilingDisabled {\n     param([object]$Config = $null)\n     # Default-disabled: the old direct deep filing is retired in favor of the adversarial VERIFY pipeline.\n     if ($null -ne $Config -and $null -ne $Config.PSObject.Properties[\u0027directDeepFilingDisabled\u0027]) {\n       return [bool]$Config.directDeepFilingDisabled\n     }\n     return $true\n   }\n\n2) At the TOP of Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog (right after the initial counter inits like $deepFiled = 0, BEFORE any filing loop), insert an early-return guard:\n   if (Test-AuditDirectDeepFilingDisabled) {\n     try { Write-AuditLog -BridgePath $Root -Message \u0027deep-audit direct filing disabled -- deep findings now route through adversarial VERIFY (Invoke-AuditFileConfirmed in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1)\u0027 } catch {}\n     return [pscustomobject]@{ deepFiled = 0; deepCodexCount = 0; deepClaudeCount = 0; deepModelAgentCount = 0 }\n   }\n   This preserves the exact return shape the call site reads, so nothing downstream breaks. Leave the rest of the function intact (reversible: flip the helper to re-enable if ever needed).\n\n3) Update the stale TODO comment in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 (line ~113 \u0027TODO Phase 6: Neutralize Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog in tools/audit.ps1:1441.\u0027) to note it is DONE: change it to a DONE/comment line stating the neutralization is implemented via Test-AuditDirectDeepFilingDisabled in tools/audit.ps1.\n\nAdd tools/test-audit-deep-filing-disabled.ps1 (new file):\n   - Assert [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile on tools/audit.ps1 yields zero errors (PS5.1 clean).\n   - Dot-source tools/audit.ps1 (safe: main-guarded). After dot-sourcing, define stubs: function Write-AuditLog {} and a tracking Add-Idea: function Add-Idea { $script:addIdeaCalled = $true; return \u0027STUB\u0027 }. Set $script:addIdeaCalled = $false.\n   - Assert Test-AuditDirectDeepFilingDisabled returns $true by default; and with -Config ([pscustomobject]@{ directDeepFilingDisabled = $false }) returns $false.\n   - Build a dummy $ctx = [pscustomobject]@{ kind=\u0027bridge\u0027; backlog_channel=\u0027main\u0027 } and a dummy deep result $dc = [pscustomobject]@{ findings = @([pscustomobject]@{ severity=\u0027critical\u0027; category=\u0027x\u0027; file=\u0027f.ps1\u0027; line=1; finding=\u0027y\u0027; recommendation=\u0027z\u0027 }) }. Call: $r = Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog -Root (Get-Location).Path -AuditCtx $ctx -DeepCodexResult $dc -DeepClaudeResult $null -DeepModelAgentResults @() -AddIdeaAvailable $true -Errors ([ref]([System.Collections.ArrayList]::new())).\n   - Assert $r.deepFiled -eq 0 AND $script:addIdeaCalled -eq $false (the bypass is closed: no Add-Idea call, nothing filed despite a critical finding being present).\n\nBoth .ps1 must ParseFile clean (PS5.1); the test prints PASS per case + final count, then commit. Reference: project_map_plan.md section 11 (old direct filing must be disabled or routed through confirmed_only) + section 13 Phase 6 (retire old deep path; nightly static unchanged).\n","commit":"0e7d3e52f2c44b04e2e912eefa2adcd1e799efe9","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-25T11:30:50.4124642Z"}
