{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":150.94,"success_pct":0.99},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] Fix a CRITICAL bug in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1: grounded findings never get a finding_id, so VERIFY vote-matching is broken and every finding resolves to \u0027unverified\u0027. Also fix quorum.valid_count counting abstains. Surgical change + NON-FIXTURE test + commit.\n\n[[NORMAL]]\n\n[operator] Context (verified): findings from the real finder schema (Test-AuditFinderSchema) carry dimension/agent_id/file/line/evidence_snippet but NO finding_id. Invoke-AuditGroundingGate (line ~511) only adds state+grounding_reason. So in Invoke-AuditVerifyStage, Build-AuditSkepticJobSpec reads $Finding.finding_id = empty (line 551), and the vote-\u003efinding match at line 675 compares \u0027\u0027==\u0027\u0027 for every finding -\u003e votes mis-correlate and Resolve-AuditFindingVerdict always returns \u0027unverified\u0027. The e2e/verify-stage tests only passed because they hand-inject finding_id (a fixture the real schema never produces).\n\nMake these changes to tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 (do NOT break other functions):\n\n1) Add a helper Get-AuditFindingId -Finding \u003cobject\u003e:\n   - Deterministic stable id from STRUCTURE: SHA1 hex (first 16 chars ok) of the string  \"$([string]$Finding.file)|$([string]$Finding.line)|$([string]$Finding.dimension)|$([string]$Finding.evidence_snippet)|$([string]$Finding.agent_id)\" (whitespace-normalized like Get-AuditFindingStructuralKey does). Return the hex string.\n\n2) In Invoke-AuditGroundingGate: when building each finding copy ($fCopy), in ADDITION to state+grounding_reason, add a finding_id via Add-Member -NotePropertyName \u0027finding_id\u0027 (only if the finding does not already have a non-empty finding_id; if it already has one, keep it). Do this for BOTH grounded and rejected_grounding copies so every returned finding carries a stable finding_id.\n\n3) Defensive in Invoke-AuditVerifyStage: at the very start of the foreach that builds job specs (and before the result foreach), ensure each grounded finding has a non-empty finding_id; if missing, assign via Get-AuditFindingId and write it onto the finding object (Add-Member -Force) so both the jobspec build (line ~551) and the vote match (line ~675) use the same id.\n\n4) Fix quorum.valid_count to match the verdict\u0027s count (which EXCLUDES abstains): change the $validVotes computation (line ~677) to also exclude abstains:\n   $validVotes = @($votesForF | Where-Object { (Test-AuditSkepticSchema -Obj $_).valid -and ([string]$_.vote) -ne \u0027abstain\u0027 })\n   (refute_count/support_count derive from this, which is already correct; this makes quorum.valid_count equal the decisive non-abstain count.)\n\nAdd tools/test-adversarial-verify-idwiring.ps1 (NEW file — NON-FIXTURE: build findings the way the REAL finder schema produces them, i.e. WITH dimension+agent_id and WITHOUT any finding_id):\n   - Build 2 findings as pscustomobjects with fields: root_cause, file=\u0027sample.ps1\u0027, line (2 and 3), evidence_snippet, severity=\u0027high\u0027/\u0027low\u0027, why, fix_sketch, confidence=0.9, dimension=\u0027correctness\u0027/\u0027security\u0027, agent_id=\u0027a1\u0027/\u0027a2\u0027. NO finding_id property.\n   - Create a temp snapshot dir with sample.ps1 (5+ lines) so both findings are grounded; run them through Invoke-AuditGroundingGate -SnapshotRoot \u003ctemp\u003e.\n   - Assert: each grounded finding now HAS a non-empty finding_id, and the two finding_ids are DIFFERENT.\n   - Run Invoke-AuditVerifyStage on the grounded findings with a -VoteCollector that, for each jobSpec, returns a vote object echoing jobSpec.finding_id with: finding #1 -\u003e [support,support,refute] (expect confirmed), finding #2 -\u003e [refute,refute,support] (expect refuted). The collector MUST read finding_id from the jobSpecs (proving real correlation, not a hand-picked literal).\n   - Assert: finding #1 verdict==\u0027confirmed\u0027, finding #2 verdict==\u0027refuted\u0027 (this would FAIL on the old code where all were \u0027unverified\u0027).\n   - Add one abstain case: a third grounded finding with votes [support(valid), abstain, abstain], MinValidVotes=2 -\u003e verdict \u0027unverified\u0027 AND quorum.valid_count==1 (NOT 3) — proving abstains are excluded from the reported count.\n\nBoth .ps1 must ParseFile clean (PS5.1); the test prints PASS per case + final count, then commit. This closes the false-green that fixtures masked.\n","commit":"eacb9bd4cb5cd6d7ece398b0ff7edfdb9ccdf8e6","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-25T12:16:06.3515983Z"}
