{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":159.62,"success_pct":0.99},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] Fix finder-input robustness in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1: (#5) the finder JSON extractor drops a real finding when reasoning prose contains a stray brace; (#1/#2) tighten the over-permissive NumberStyles::Any line/confidence validation introduced earlier. Surgical + test update + commit.\n\n[[NORMAL]]\n\n[operator] Make these changes to tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 (do NOT break other functions):\n\n#5 — ConvertFrom-AuditFinderOutput must scan candidate JSON spans, not commit to the first brace/bracket:\n - Today it takes the FIRST \u0027{\u0027 or \u0027[\u0027 only, depth-matches that one span, and returns @() if it fails to parse — so a stray \u0027{\u0027 in prose before the real JSON loses the finding.\n - Change it to iterate over candidate start positions in ascending index order: collect every index of \u0027{\u0027 and \u0027[\u0027 in $Text; for each candidate (earliest first), depth-match the balanced span starting there and try ConvertFrom-Json; RETURN the parsed result (object or array, normalized to an array) for the FIRST candidate that parses successfully. Only return @() after all candidates fail. Keep existing depth-matching logic; just wrap it in a loop over candidate starts with try/catch per candidate.\n\n#1 — line validation: replace the NumberStyles::Any double-parse with an INTEGER parse consistent with the grounding gate ([int]::TryParse). In Test-AuditFinderSchema:\n   $lineInt = 0\n   $okLine = [int]::TryParse([string]$lineVal, [System.Globalization.NumberStyles]::Integer, [System.Globalization.CultureInfo]::InvariantCulture, [ref]$lineInt)\n   valid only if $okLine -and $lineInt -ge 1  (reason \u0027line must be a positive integer\u0027). This rejects thousands-separators, exponents, decimals (e.g. \u00275.0\u0027), NaN/Infinity, and out-of-Int32 garbage like 3000000000 — matching what the grounding gate\u0027s [int]::TryParse accepts, so no finding passes schema only to die at grounding.\n\n#2 — confidence validation: use NumberStyles::Float (not ::Any) to drop thousands-separators/exponent/special values while keeping normal decimals and leading sign:\n   $confD = 0.0\n   $okConf = [double]::TryParse([string]$confVal, [System.Globalization.NumberStyles]::Float, [System.Globalization.CultureInfo]::InvariantCulture, [ref]$confD)\n   valid only if $okConf -and $confD -ge 0 -and $confD -le 1.\n\nUPDATE tools/test-adversarial-hardening.ps1 (the C-section assertions must reflect the corrected, grounding-consistent contract — flip the now-rejected cases):\n - line=3000000000 -\u003e INVALID (out of Int32 / garbage); line=5.0 -\u003e INVALID (decimal, consistent with grounding); line=\u00271,234\u0027 -\u003e INVALID; line=\u00271e3\u0027 -\u003e INVALID.\n - line=\u002742\u0027 (string) -\u003e valid; line=42 (int) -\u003e valid; line=1 -\u003e valid.\n - confidence=\u00270.9\u0027 (string) -\u003e valid; confidence=0.9 -\u003e valid; confidence=\u00271,000\u0027 -\u003e INVALID; confidence=\u0027NaN\u0027 -\u003e INVALID.\n - KEEP the existing B (dimension key) and E (severity normalization) assertions unchanged.\n - ADD #5 parse-scan cases: ConvertFrom-AuditFinderOutput on text where a stray \u0027{ a = 1 }\u0027 precedes a valid finding object `{...valid...}` -\u003e returns the VALID finding (count 1), not @(); and on text where prose \u0027[x]\u0027 precedes a valid array `[{...valid...}]` -\u003e recovers the valid finding.\n\nBoth .ps1 must ParseFile clean (PS5.1); test prints PASS per case + final count, then commit. Reference: re-review findings #5/#1/#2.\n","commit":"74c9be76044648d7f17ffd9cdcd138dc6b0f5d53","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-25T14:37:56.6238871Z"}
