{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":159.28,"success_pct":0.99},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] Fix the claude skeptic CLI invocation in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1: it is built WITHOUT -p (print mode), so real claude skeptics never emit parseable JSON on stdout and silently abstain, halving effective quorum. Surgical + test flip + commit.\n\n[[NORMAL]]\n\n[operator] In tools/adversarial-audit.ps1, function New-AuditCliJobSpec, the claude branch currently builds:\n   $argList = @(\u0027--add-dir\u0027, $SnapshotRoot, \u0027--allowedTools\u0027, \u0027Read,Grep,Glob\u0027, \u0027--model\u0027, $Model)\nThis lacks -p/--print, so claude does not run in non-interactive print mode and will not print the bare JSON vote on stdout that Invoke-AuditVerifyStage parses. Every other claude invocation in the repo that pipes a prompt via stdin uses -p (e.g. driver/40-agent-invoke.ps1, lib/parallel.ps1).\n\nChange the claude branch to prepend -p (keep the prompt in inputText / stdin as today):\n   $argList = @(\u0027-p\u0027, \u0027--add-dir\u0027, $SnapshotRoot, \u0027--allowedTools\u0027, \u0027Read,Grep,Glob\u0027, \u0027--model\u0027, $Model)\nDo NOT change the codex branch.\n\nUPDATE tools/test-adversarial-provider.ps1: it currently ASSERTS that the claude argumentList does NOT contain \u0027-p\u0027 (a pinned assertion, message like \"claude prompt must stay in inputText, not -p\"). FLIP that assertion to require the corrected behavior:\n - assert the claude spec argumentList CONTAINS \u0027-p\u0027;\n - assert the claude spec inputText -eq the prompt (prompt still delivered via stdin, NOT as a positional arg);\n - keep the existing assertions that gemini/other providers are rejected and that codex uses \u0027-o\u0027.\n\nBoth .ps1 must ParseFile clean (PS5.1); the test prints PASS per case + final count, then commit. Reference: re-review finding #7 (claude skeptics silently abstain without -p).\n","commit":"df6d2e75a0ec0e91a167b18250eb919316bc0ff7","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-25T14:54:41.0964648Z"}
