{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":165.18,"success_pct":0.99},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] Wire the real FIND stage in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 so the adversarial audit can actually dispatch Claude/Codex finder agents across the dimension x perspective matrix through the read-only pool (this is where \u003e=20 parallel agents happen). Mirror the VERIFY stage\u0027s dispatch pattern. Straight implementation + test (seam) + commit.\n\n[[NORMAL]]\n\n[operator] Today Invoke-AdversarialAudit\u0027s FIND stage returns @() unless an injected -FindRunner is given (real dispatch was deferred). Add the real dispatch (keep -FindRunner as a top-level test override).\n\nAdd to tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 (reuse New-AuditCliJobSpec, ConvertFrom-AuditFinderOutput, Test-AuditFinderSchema, Start-ReadOnlyAuditJob/Wait-ReadOnlyAuditPoolDrain like Invoke-AuditVerifyStage already does):\n\n1) Build-AuditFinderJobSpec -Dimension \u003cstring\u003e -Perspective \u003cobject\u003e -SnapshotRoot \u003cpath\u003e -Provider \u003cclaude|codex\u003e -Index \u003cint\u003e:\n   - Reject providers other than claude/codex (throw).\n   - $agentId = \"$Provider-$Dimension-$Index\".\n   - Build a finder prompt instructing the agent to audit the code under the snapshot for the given dimension (and perspective hint) and return STRICT JSON: an ARRAY of finding objects, each with EXACTLY these fields: root_cause, file (path relative to snapshot root), line (positive integer), evidence_snippet (a short exact substring of the cited line), severity (one of critical/high/medium/low/info), why, fix_sketch, confidence (0..1), dimension (=\u0027$Dimension\u0027), agent_id (=\u0027$agentId\u0027). Return [pscustomobject]@{ dimension; provider; index; agent_id; prompt; snapshot_root }.\n\n2) Invoke-AuditFindStage -Matrix \u003cobject\u003e -SnapshotRoot \u003cpath\u003e [-MaxFinders 24] [-JobRunner \u003cscriptblock\u003e]:\n   - Enumerate the matrix into (dimension, perspective) cells. For each cell build a Build-AuditFinderJobSpec, alternating provider claude/codex by index, capping the total at MaxFinders (log if capped).\n   - Obtain raw outputs: if -JobRunner provided -\u003e $outputs = @(\u0026 $JobRunner $jobSpecs) (test seam: returns an array of stdout strings, one per jobSpec in order). Else dispatch each spec through the read-only pool exactly like Invoke-AuditVerifyStage does: create a temp $resultPath; New-AuditCliJobSpec -Provider $spec.provider -SnapshotRoot $spec.snapshot_root -Prompt $spec.prompt -ResultPath $resultPath; Start-ReadOnlyAuditJob -FilePath/-ArgumentList/-WorkingDirectory/-InputText with -Metadata @{ provider=$spec.provider; dimension=$spec.dimension; agent_id=$spec.agent_id; result_path=$resultPath }; Wait-ReadOnlyAuditPoolDrain; then read each job\u0027s output via the PROVIDER-AWARE reader `Read-AuditJobOutput -Record $record` (so codex finders are read from their -o result file, NOT stdout — same fix as VERIFY). Parse each output text with ConvertFrom-AuditFinderOutput.\n   - For each (spec, output) pair: ConvertFrom-AuditFinderOutput $output -\u003e for each parsed finding, if it lacks dimension set it to $spec.dimension, if it lacks agent_id set it to $spec.agent_id; collect.\n   - Return ALL parsed findings (schema filtering happens in the orchestrator as today). Also expose a count of finder jobs dispatched.\n\n3) Wire Invoke-AdversarialAudit FIND stage: add params [scriptblock]$FindJobRunner = $null and [int]$MaxFinders = 24. Replace the FIND stub so that:\n   - if $FindRunner provided -\u003e $rawFindings = @(\u0026 $FindRunner $matrix $SnapshotRoot)   (unchanged; existing tests rely on this)\n   - elseif real/seam -\u003e $rawFindings = @(Invoke-AuditFindStage -Matrix $matrix -SnapshotRoot $SnapshotRoot -MaxFinders $MaxFinders -JobRunner $FindJobRunner)\n   Keep the existing schema-validation filter on $rawFindings afterwards. Add finder_jobs count into the returned phases object.\n\nAdd tools/test-adversarial-findstage.ps1 (NEW file — uses -JobRunner seam, NO real CLI):\n   - Build a matrix via Get-AuditFindMatrix (default).\n   - Build a -JobRunner that returns, for each jobSpec, a JSON array string with ONE finding that OMITS dimension+agent_id (to prove the stage stamps them from the spec) but includes the other 8 schema fields with file/line/evidence valid.\n   - Call Invoke-AuditFindStage -Matrix $m -SnapshotRoot \u0027C:/x\u0027 -MaxFinders 6 -JobRunner $jr.\n   - Assert: result count == number of dispatched jobs (\u003c=6); every returned finding has a non-empty dimension AND agent_id (stamped from the spec); at least one provider is \u0027claude\u0027 and one is \u0027codex\u0027 in the specs (alternation). Build-AuditFinderJobSpec -Provider \u0027gemini\u0027 throws.\n   - Also assert Invoke-AdversarialAudit with -FindJobRunner (and NO -FindRunner) on a tiny temp snapshot produces find_raw\u003e=1 and reaches grounding (proves the wiring path), using a -VoteCollector + -Filer seam to complete the run.\n\nBoth .ps1 must ParseFile clean (PS5.1); the test prints PASS per case + final count, then commit. Reference: project_map_plan.md sections 4 (FIND) + 13 Phase 2/3 dispatch; mirror Invoke-AuditVerifyStage\u0027s pool usage.\n","commit":"00b07f0e25f19017f61013c8e99ef476697f023c","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-25T16:31:17.2723034Z"}
