{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":82.81,"success_pct":0.01},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] Neutralize the old direct deep-audit backlog filing in tools/audit.ps1 so unverified deep findings can no longer bypass the adversarial VERIFY stage. Small surgical change + test + commit. Do NOT touch the static-audit filing path.\n\n[[NORMAL]]\n\n[operator] Context: tools/audit.ps1 function Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog (starts line 1441) files ONLY deep-LLM findings (DeepCodexResult/DeepClaudeResult/DeepModelAgentResults) directly to the backlog, bypassing the new VERIFY pipeline. It returns [pscustomobject]@{ deepFiled; deepCodexCount; deepClaudeCount; deepModelAgentCount }. The call site (~line 1881) reads those four properties. audit.ps1 has a main-guard at the bottom (if InvocationName -ne \u0027.\u0027) so dot-sourcing is SAFE (main does not run).\n\nMake these changes to tools/audit.ps1 (do NOT break static-audit filing, which is a separate path):\n\n1) Add a small pure helper near Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog:\n   function Test-AuditDirectDeepFilingDisabled {\n     param([object]$Config = $null)\n     # Default-disabled: the old direct deep filing is retired in favor of the adversarial VERIFY pipeline.\n     if ($null -ne $Config -and $null -ne $Config.PSObject.Properties[\u0027directDeepFilingDisabled\u0027]) {\n       return [bool]$Config.directDeepFilingDisabled\n     }\n     return $true\n   }\n\n2) At the TOP of Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog (right after the initial counter inits like $deepFiled = 0, BEFORE any filing loop), insert an early-return guard:\n   if (Test-AuditDirectDeepFilingDisabled) {\n     try { Write-AuditLog -BridgePath $Root -Message \u0027deep-audit direct filing disabled -- deep findings now route through adversarial VERIFY (Invoke-AuditFileConfirmed in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1)\u0027 } catch {}\n     return [pscustomobject]@{ deepFiled = 0; deepCodexCount = 0; deepClaudeCount = 0; deepModelAgentCount = 0 }\n   }\n   This preserves the exact return shape the call site reads, so nothing downstream breaks. Leave the rest of the function intact (reversible: flip the helper to re-enable if ever needed).\n\n3) Update the stale TODO comment in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 (line ~113 \u0027TODO Phase 6: Neutralize Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog in tools/audit.ps1:1441.\u0027) to note it is DONE: change it to a DONE/comment line stating the neutralization is implemented via Test-AuditDirectDeepFilingDisabled in tools/audit.ps1.\n\nAdd tools/test-audit-deep-filing-disabled.ps1 (new file):\n   - Assert [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile on tools/audit.ps1 yields zero errors (PS5.1 clean).\n   - Dot-source tools/audit.ps1 (safe: main-guarded). After dot-sourcing, define stubs: function Write-AuditLog {} and a tracking Add-Idea: function Add-Idea { $script:addIdeaCalled = $true; return \u0027STUB\u0027 }. Set $script:addIdeaCalled = $false.\n   - Assert Test-AuditDirectDeepFilingDisabled returns $true by default; and with -Config ([pscustomobject]@{ directDeepFilingDisabled = $false }) returns $false.\n   - Build a dummy $ctx = [pscustomobject]@{ kind=\u0027bridge\u0027; backlog_channel=\u0027main\u0027 } and a dummy deep result $dc = [pscustomobject]@{ findings = @([pscustomobject]@{ severity=\u0027critical\u0027; category=\u0027x\u0027; file=\u0027f.ps1\u0027; line=1; finding=\u0027y\u0027; recommendation=\u0027z\u0027 }) }. Call: $r = Add-DeepAuditFindingsToBacklog -Root (Get-Location).Path -AuditCtx $ctx -DeepCodexResult $dc -DeepClaudeResult $null -DeepModelAgentResults @() -AddIdeaAvailable $true -Errors ([ref]([System.Collections.ArrayList]::new())).\n   - Assert $r.deepFiled -eq 0 AND $script:addIdeaCalled -eq $false (the bypass is closed: no Add-Idea call, nothing filed despite a critical finding being present).\n\nBoth .ps1 must ParseFile clean (PS5.1); the test prints PASS per case + final count, then commit. Reference: project_map_plan.md section 11 (old direct filing must be disabled or routed through confirmed_only) + section 13 Phase 6 (retire old deep path; nightly static unchanged).\n","after_turns":46,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":235.95,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-25T11:30:50.4124642Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-26T23:00:09.3454276Z","commit":"0e7d3e52f2c44b04e2e912eefa2adcd1e799efe9"}
{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":99.02,"success_pct":0.01},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] Fix a CRITICAL bug in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1: grounded findings never get a finding_id, so VERIFY vote-matching is broken and every finding resolves to \u0027unverified\u0027. Also fix quorum.valid_count counting abstains. Surgical change + NON-FIXTURE test + commit.\n\n[[NORMAL]]\n\n[operator] Context (verified): findings from the real finder schema (Test-AuditFinderSchema) carry dimension/agent_id/file/line/evidence_snippet but NO finding_id. Invoke-AuditGroundingGate (line ~511) only adds state+grounding_reason. So in Invoke-AuditVerifyStage, Build-AuditSkepticJobSpec reads $Finding.finding_id = empty (line 551), and the vote-\u003efinding match at line 675 compares \u0027\u0027==\u0027\u0027 for every finding -\u003e votes mis-correlate and Resolve-AuditFindingVerdict always returns \u0027unverified\u0027. The e2e/verify-stage tests only passed because they hand-inject finding_id (a fixture the real schema never produces).\n\nMake these changes to tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 (do NOT break other functions):\n\n1) Add a helper Get-AuditFindingId -Finding \u003cobject\u003e:\n   - Deterministic stable id from STRUCTURE: SHA1 hex (first 16 chars ok) of the string  \"$([string]$Finding.file)|$([string]$Finding.line)|$([string]$Finding.dimension)|$([string]$Finding.evidence_snippet)|$([string]$Finding.agent_id)\" (whitespace-normalized like Get-AuditFindingStructuralKey does). Return the hex string.\n\n2) In Invoke-AuditGroundingGate: when building each finding copy ($fCopy), in ADDITION to state+grounding_reason, add a finding_id via Add-Member -NotePropertyName \u0027finding_id\u0027 (only if the finding does not already have a non-empty finding_id; if it already has one, keep it). Do this for BOTH grounded and rejected_grounding copies so every returned finding carries a stable finding_id.\n\n3) Defensive in Invoke-AuditVerifyStage: at the very start of the foreach that builds job specs (and before the result foreach), ensure each grounded finding has a non-empty finding_id; if missing, assign via Get-AuditFindingId and write it onto the finding object (Add-Member -Force) so both the jobspec build (line ~551) and the vote match (line ~675) use the same id.\n\n4) Fix quorum.valid_count to match the verdict\u0027s count (which EXCLUDES abstains): change the $validVotes computation (line ~677) to also exclude abstains:\n   $validVotes = @($votesForF | Where-Object { (Test-AuditSkepticSchema -Obj $_).valid -and ([string]$_.vote) -ne \u0027abstain\u0027 })\n   (refute_count/support_count derive from this, which is already correct; this makes quorum.valid_count equal the decisive non-abstain count.)\n\nAdd tools/test-adversarial-verify-idwiring.ps1 (NEW file — NON-FIXTURE: build findings the way the REAL finder schema produces them, i.e. WITH dimension+agent_id and WITHOUT any finding_id):\n   - Build 2 findings as pscustomobjects with fields: root_cause, file=\u0027sample.ps1\u0027, line (2 and 3), evidence_snippet, severity=\u0027high\u0027/\u0027low\u0027, why, fix_sketch, confidence=0.9, dimension=\u0027correctness\u0027/\u0027security\u0027, agent_id=\u0027a1\u0027/\u0027a2\u0027. NO finding_id property.\n   - Create a temp snapshot dir with sample.ps1 (5+ lines) so both findings are grounded; run them through Invoke-AuditGroundingGate -SnapshotRoot \u003ctemp\u003e.\n   - Assert: each grounded finding now HAS a non-empty finding_id, and the two finding_ids are DIFFERENT.\n   - Run Invoke-AuditVerifyStage on the grounded findings with a -VoteCollector that, for each jobSpec, returns a vote object echoing jobSpec.finding_id with: finding #1 -\u003e [support,support,refute] (expect confirmed), finding #2 -\u003e [refute,refute,support] (expect refuted). The collector MUST read finding_id from the jobSpecs (proving real correlation, not a hand-picked literal).\n   - Assert: finding #1 verdict==\u0027confirmed\u0027, finding #2 verdict==\u0027refuted\u0027 (this would FAIL on the old code where all were \u0027unverified\u0027).\n   - Add one abstain case: a third grounded finding with votes [support(valid), abstain, abstain], MinValidVotes=2 -\u003e verdict \u0027unverified\u0027 AND quorum.valid_count==1 (NOT 3) — proving abstains are excluded from the reported count.\n\nBoth .ps1 must ParseFile clean (PS5.1); the test prints PASS per case + final count, then commit. This closes the false-green that fixtures masked.\n","after_turns":42,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":249.96,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-25T12:16:06.3515983Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-26T23:00:13.9814217Z","commit":"eacb9bd4cb5cd6d7ece398b0ff7edfdb9ccdf8e6"}
