{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":101.45,"success_pct":0.01},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] Fix three confirmed field/validation bugs in tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 found by adversarial review: (B) dedup/report read a non-existent \u0027category\u0027 field instead of \u0027dimension\u0027; (C) finder number validation is brittle (Int64 line aborts FIND, decimal/quoted numbers dropped); (E) grounding gate omits severity normalization. Surgical changes + NON-FIXTURE test + commit.\n\n[[NORMAL]]\n\n[operator] All findings carry `dimension` (finder schema), NOT `category`; numbers come from ConvertFrom-Json with varying CLR types. Make these changes to tools/adversarial-audit.ps1 (do NOT break other functions; keep existing passing tests green):\n\nPART B — use dimension, not category (category is always empty):\n 1) Get-AuditFindingStructuralKey (~line 709): change `$catPart = [string]$Finding.category` to read dimension with category fallback: `$catPart = if ([string]$Finding.dimension) { [string]$Finding.dimension } elseif ([string]$Finding.category) { [string]$Finding.category } else { \u0027\u0027 }`.\n 2) Build-AuditFixAtom (~line 31, `$category = [string]$Finding.category`): same dimension-with-category-fallback.\n 3) The Markdown report section in Invoke-AuditSynthesize (~line 787 referencing `$f.category`): same dimension-with-category-fallback so report headers are not blank.\n\nPART C — tolerant numeric validation in Test-AuditFinderSchema (currently uses brittle `-is [int]/[long]/[double]` + `[int]$lineVal`, which throws OverflowException on Int64 and drops decimals/quoted numbers):\n 4) Replace the `line` validation: accept any value that parses as a positive integer via double TryParse (invariant culture), tolerating Int64 and decimal/quoted forms but rejecting non-integers:\n    $lineD = 0.0; $okLine = [double]::TryParse([string]$lineVal, [System.Globalization.NumberStyles]::Any, [System.Globalization.CultureInfo]::InvariantCulture, [ref]$lineD)\n    valid only if $okLine AND $lineD -ge 1 AND $lineD -eq [math]::Floor($lineD). (No [int] cast anywhere — avoids overflow.)\n 5) Replace the `confidence` validation similarly: $confD=0.0; $okConf=[double]::TryParse([string]$confVal, Any, InvariantCulture, [ref]$confD); valid only if $okConf AND $confD -ge 0 AND $confD -le 1. (Accepts 0.9 and \"0.9\".)\n 6) Wrap the per-finding schema check at the FIND call site in Invoke-AdversarialAudit (~line 878, the `Where-Object { (Test-AuditFinderSchema -Obj $_).valid }` filter) so a single throwing finding cannot abort the whole batch: filter via a try/catch that treats a throwing item as invalid (dropped), not fatal.\n\nPART E — normalize severity in the grounding gate (plan section 5, 4th check):\n 7) In Invoke-AuditGroundingGate, on each finding copy, normalize severity: write back `severity` = lowercased trimmed value (Add-Member -Force). Accept set {critical,high,medium,low,info}; if the lowercased value is not in the set, leave it as the lowercased original (do not drop — schema already gates membership upstream).\n\nAdd tools/test-adversarial-hardening.ps1 (NEW file — NON-FIXTURE, exercise the REAL field names):\n - B: two confirmed-style findings, same file+evidence_snippet, DIFFERENT dimension (\u0027correctness\u0027 vs \u0027security\u0027), NO category field -\u003e Get-AuditFindingStructuralKey returns TWO DIFFERENT keys (assert not equal); Build-AuditFixAtom text contains the dimension token (not empty brackets `[]`).\n - C: Test-AuditFinderSchema on a complete finding with line=3000000000 -\u003e valid (no exception); line=5.0 -\u003e valid; line=\u002742\u0027 (string) -\u003e valid; confidence=\u00270.9\u0027 (string) -\u003e valid; line=\u0027abc\u0027 -\u003e invalid; line=5.5 -\u003e invalid; line=0 -\u003e invalid. Also: a batch of 3 findings where one has line=3000000000 passed through the same `try/catch` filter pattern used at the call site does NOT throw and keeps the valid ones.\n - E: build a finding with severity=\u0027Critical\u0027, run Invoke-AuditGroundingGate against a temp snapshot where it grounds -\u003e the returned finding\u0027s severity -eq \u0027critical\u0027 (lowercased).\n\nBoth .ps1 must ParseFile clean (PS5.1); the test prints PASS per case + final count, then commit. Reference: adversarial review findings B/C/E + project_map_plan.md sections 5, 11.\n","after_turns":39,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":253.87,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-25T12:42:58.7059039Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-26T23:00:19.8239606Z","commit":"f468d9795adebd3d66f47c077961a334c0e84afe"}
